        "tipo": "gramatica",
        "min": 12,
        "titulo": "Asking for and giving directions (formal imperative)",
        "explicacao": "To ask: «Entschuldigung, wo ist die Post?» (Excuse me, where's the post office?) or «Wie komme ich zum Bahnhof?» (How do I get to the station?). To answer, use the formal imperative: the verb comes FIRST, followed by «Sie»: «Gehen Sie geradeaus.» (Go straight ahead.) «Biegen Sie links ab.» (Turn left — «abbiegen» is separable, so the prefix goes to the end.) «Nehmen Sie die zweite Straße rechts.» (Take the second street on the right.) English drops the \"you\" in commands; German formal commands keep «Sie». Other useful phrases: an der Ampel (at the light), an der Kreuzung (at the intersection), neben (next to), gegenüber (across from), in der Nähe (nearby).",
